From: Pyra kernel work <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: ti: aess: enable the McPDM back-end ports

enable_be_port() and disable_be_port() skipped all three McPDM back ends
with the comment "McPDM is a special case, handled by McPDM driver". No
driver in this tree handles it. sound/soc/ti/omap-mcpdm.c knows nothing
about the AESS port manager, and the unbuilt sound/soc/omap/ -- where the
rest of the stranded AESS code was recovered from -- has no mcpdm.c at all.

So omap_aess_enable_data_transfer() never ran for PDM_DL1. The DSP's
downlink processing tasks are written into MultiFrame by the port enable
path, so they were never dispatched: the front end ran, the DL1 buffer in
SMEM filled, and McPDM faithfully transmitted the silence it was handed.
Observed directly -- with a stream running, debugfs showed mm_dl_lp at
PORT_ENABLED and pdmdl1 still PORT_DISABLED.

Patch 0022 opened these ports; this enables them. They need no port
configuration: unlike BT_VX and MM_EXT there is no serial port to connect,
so this matches the DMIC cases immediately below.
---
--- a/sound/soc/ti/aess/omap-aess-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/aess/omap-aess-dai.c
@@ -193,10 +193,25 @@
 	dev_dbg(be->dev, "%s: %s %d\n", __func__, be->cpu_dai->name, stream);
 
 	switch (be->dai_link->id) {
+	/*
+	 * The comment these three used to carry said McPDM was "handled by
+	 * McPDM driver". No driver in this tree handles it: sound/soc/ti/
+	 * omap-mcpdm.c knows nothing about the AESS port manager, and the
+	 * unbuilt sound/soc/omap/ has no mcpdm.c at all. So nothing ever
+	 * called omap_aess_enable_data_transfer() for the PDM ports, the
+	 * DSP's downlink tasks were never dispatched, and McPDM faithfully
+	 * transmitted the silence it was handed. Enable them here with the
+	 * rest. They need no port configuration -- unlike BT_VX and MM_EXT
+	 * there is no serial port to connect, so this matches the DMIC case.
+	 */
 	case OMAP_AESS_BE_ID_PDM_DL1:
+		omap_aess_port_enable(aess, OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_DL1);
+		break;
 	case OMAP_AESS_BE_ID_PDM_DL2:
+		omap_aess_port_enable(aess, OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_DL2);
+		break;
 	case OMAP_AESS_BE_ID_PDM_UL:
-		/* McPDM is a special case, handled by McPDM driver */
+		omap_aess_port_enable(aess, OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_UL1);
 		break;
 	case OMAP_AESS_BE_ID_BT_VX:
 		if (stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK) {
@@ -322,10 +337,15 @@
 	dev_dbg(be->dev, "%s: %s %d\n", __func__, be->cpu_dai->name, stream);
 
 	switch (be->dai_link->id) {
-	/* McPDM is a special case, handled by McPDM driver */
+	/* See enable_be_port(): nothing else disables these either. */
 	case OMAP_AESS_BE_ID_PDM_DL1:
+		omap_aess_port_disable(aess, OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_DL1);
+		break;
 	case OMAP_AESS_BE_ID_PDM_DL2:
+		omap_aess_port_disable(aess, OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_DL2);
+		break;
 	case OMAP_AESS_BE_ID_PDM_UL:
+		omap_aess_port_disable(aess, OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_UL1);
 		break;
 	case OMAP_AESS_BE_ID_BT_VX:
 		if (stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK)
